        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kabsa is built on a fragrant "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "baharat-blend"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "baharat blend"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " that flavours both the chicken braising liquid and the rice. The rice is finished using the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "absorption-cooking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "absorption method"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in the strained chicken broth, so every grain carries the spice. The fried onion and nut garnish is part of the dish, not optional."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: measure the strained broth carefully before adding the rice. The ratio matters for fluffy, separate grains."
          }
        ]
      },
